[20.081438, "o", "Warning: running headless with --yolo / approval-mode=yolo and no sandbox. All tool calls (shell, write, edit) auto-execute at this process's privilege level. Configure tools.executionSandbox on Linux or a supported legacy sandbox via --sandbox / QWEN_SANDBOX, or set QWEN_CODE_SUPPRESS_YOLO_WARNING=1 to silence this notice.\r\n"]
[629.419307, "o", "The mailing list server is up and working. Summary of what was configured:\r\n\r\n**Mailman 3** (`/etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg`)\r\n- `site_owner` set to `postmaster@local.edu`.\r\n- Existing Postfix integration kept: LMTP on `127.0.0.1:8024`, outgoing SMTP to `localhost:25`, Postfix alias generation via `python:mailman.config.postfix`.\r\n- List `reading-group@local.edu` created in `/var/lib/mailman3/data/mailman.db` with:\r\n  - `subscription_policy = open` (no owner approval; users still confirm by reply)\r\n  - `unsubscription_policy = confirm` (leave requires a reply confirmation)\r\n  - `default_member_action`/`default_nonmember_action = accept` (no post moderation)\r\n  - archiving disabled, subject prefix removed so announcement subjects pass through unchanged.\r\n\r\n**Postfix** (`/etc/postfix/main.cf`)\r\n- `myhostname = local.edu`, `local.edu` in `mydestination` → direct user mail is delivered to `/var/mail/<username>`.\r\n- `transport_maps = hash:/var/lib/mailman3/data/postfix_lmtp` → list, `-join`, `-leave`, `-confirm+token`, etc. addresses route to Mailman's LMTP.\r\n- `local_recipient_maps` includes the Mailman hash map; chroot disabled for all services so the map is readable; logging to `/var/log/mail.log`.\r\n\r\n**Verification**\r\n- Postfix (PID 1484) and Mailman master (PID 1573, with all runners + REST API) are running; ports 25, 8024, 8001 are open.\r\n- `/app/eval.py` passes end-to-end (direct delivery, list existence, join + confirm).\r\n- I also verified the full join → post-to-subscriber → leave + confirm cycle, including confirmation mail arriving in `/var/mail/<user>` and membership being added/removed. Test accounts were cleaned up afterward, leaving the list empty and ready.\r\n"]
